      "title": "Emmanuel College \n\tJob Posting: Assistant Director of Athletic Communications",
      "description": "Emmanuel College\nJob Posting: Assistant Director of Athletic Communications Emmanuel College \n\tJob Posting: Assistant Director of Athletic Communications Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Assistant Director of Athletic Communications Category: Athletics Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Athletics Locations: Boston, MA Posted: Sep 3, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Position ID: 204414 Share About Emmanuel College: Emmanuel College-a Catholic, coeducational, residential, liberal arts and sciences college in Boston-has been educating critical thinkers, ethical decision makers and community leaders since 1919. Situated in Boston's Fenway neighborhood within the Longwood Medical and Academic Area, Emmanuel's 17-acre campus is home to nearly 2,000 undergraduate and graduate students. The College provides boundless opportunities for students to expand their worldview through rigorous coursework, significant internship and career opportunities throughout the Boston area and beyond, collaborations with distinguished and dedicated faculty, and participation in a dynamic campus community. Emmanuel's more than 70 programs in the arts, humanities, education, natural sciences, business and nursing foster spirited discourse and substantive learning experiences that honor the College's commitment to educate the whole person and prepare students to emerge as tomorrow's leaders. For more information, visit www.emmanuel.edu. Job Description: This externally funded position, reporting to the Director of Athletic Communications and Compliance, will support and develop sports information initiatives within the department and aid in game day management, coordinate game day student workers/staff, facilitate emerging partnership with sports management programs and assist in department coordination. Essential responsibilities will include: To aid and assist the Athletics department in promotion and coverage for all varsity sports as assigned. To develop and manage digital communications/media accounts from the department in support of the Director of Athletic Communications Support and direct game day operations Facilitate partnership and pre-internship opportunities for sports management Additional staff duties as assigned by the Director of Athletics. This is a 10-month position working August through May. Requirements: Our ideal candidate will  have a Bachelor's degree and a demonstrated commitment to high academic standards and healthy lifestyles for student-athletes.  Candidates must have sports information experience and a passion for the profession of sports information and promotion through social media, web content, video stories, press releases and strategic communications. Additional Information: Emmanuel College seeks to create a working and learning environment that reflect the society and community in which we are located, and we actively encourage candidates of all backgrounds to apply. Unless otherwise stated above, this is an on-campus position. This is not a remote or hybrid position as employees are essential in order to provide a fully on-campus, residential college experience for our students and the community. The posted salary range reflects the good-faith compensation estimate for this position. The actual pay offered will be based on the candidate's skills, qualifications, experience, and internal equity factors.  This is an externally funded position with a salary range  of $50,000-$55,000. Application Instructions: A complete application must include a cover letter, resume, a statement of purpose, and contact information for three references. In your statement of purpose, please describe how your values, experiences, and professional goals align with Emmanuel College's mission to educate and inspire students in the spirit of the Sisters of Notre Dame de Namur, who are committed to social justice, human dignity, and transformative education for all. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Emmanuel College 400 The Fenway, Boston, MA 02115"
